1
00:00:13,571 --> 00:00:21,373
[SPEAKER_00]: So, these are some more questions that have come from around the world and some comments from YouTube.

2
00:00:23,574 --> 00:00:27,054
[SPEAKER_00]: I'll just read out someone's comment from YouTube.

3
00:00:30,155 --> 00:00:35,917
[SPEAKER_00]: He says, I was thinking, this person said something I heard and I didn't like.

4
00:00:37,177 --> 00:00:40,658
[SPEAKER_00]: This person did something I saw and I didn't like.

5
00:00:41,786 --> 00:00:48,067
[SPEAKER_00]: But without my eye or my ears or this body, I wouldn't be able to experience that person.

6
00:00:49,208 --> 00:00:53,849
[SPEAKER_00]: So, do I hate this person or do I really hate my eye, my ear or this body?

7
00:00:55,149 --> 00:00:59,310
[SPEAKER_00]: The world outside of this body is only experienced through this body.

8
00:01:00,130 --> 00:01:01,750
[SPEAKER_00]: So, how can it be outside?

9
00:01:03,051 --> 00:01:09,052
[SPEAKER_00]: And how can I conceive outside of this body if it's not on the basis of this same body and senses?

10
00:01:10,192 --> 00:01:13,275
[SPEAKER_00]: This is where the misconceiving happens, isn't it?

11
00:01:13,496 --> 00:01:13,716
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

12
00:01:14,777 --> 00:01:15,177
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

13
00:01:15,437 --> 00:01:17,740
[SPEAKER_01]: It's exactly what happens.

14
00:01:17,820 --> 00:01:27,410
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why the Buddha described the sense organs as hollow, empty, without a substance.

15
00:01:28,971 --> 00:01:30,473
[SPEAKER_01]: In other words, they don't appear.

16
00:01:32,395 --> 00:01:33,676
[SPEAKER_01]: You don't... you can't see your eye.

17
00:01:35,398 --> 00:01:42,365
[SPEAKER_01]: So that's why you naturally then, think you hate that which you've seen, because there is nothing else there that you can visibly hate.

18
00:01:43,706 --> 00:01:48,991
[SPEAKER_01]: But actually, what you are averse to, is the... that...

19
00:01:51,040 --> 00:01:52,682
[SPEAKER_01]: negative sense base.

20
00:01:53,524 --> 00:01:55,086
[SPEAKER_01]: It's hollow, empty.

21
00:01:55,226 --> 00:01:58,531
[SPEAKER_01]: If a man, as we say, if a man were to look closely, they will find no substance to it.

22
00:01:58,611 --> 00:01:59,672
[SPEAKER_01]: It's just devoid of...

23
00:01:59,953 --> 00:02:02,096
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's this basically a negative space of you.

24
00:02:02,176 --> 00:02:03,097
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what your eye is.

25
00:02:03,237 --> 00:02:06,081
[SPEAKER_01]: That which is... which doesn't appear where your sights are there.

26
00:02:06,842 --> 00:02:08,042
[SPEAKER_01]: But it's the reason for your sights.

27
00:02:08,402 --> 00:02:09,463
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's why it takes knowledge.

28
00:02:09,963 --> 00:02:14,804
[SPEAKER_01]: First, it takes sensory strength to stop acting towards what you see, hear, smell, taste, touch.

29
00:02:15,484 --> 00:02:18,985
[SPEAKER_01]: Stop fortifying the wrong notion that that's what you are averse to.

30
00:02:19,685 --> 00:02:28,787
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, you discover that natural aversion, natural patiga towards these senses, because they were always the untamed animals, not the objects they were seeking.

31
00:02:29,752 --> 00:02:32,674
[SPEAKER_01]: But even then, you will not see the eye as an object.

32
00:02:32,994 --> 00:02:34,334
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, now I recognize you.

33
00:02:34,715 --> 00:02:48,062
[SPEAKER_01]: But you get to know that through withdrawal from the sense objects that I used to chase with likes or dislikes, what I'm left with now is that pure aversion to the fact that there is seeing there that undermines me, that I'm subjected to...

34
00:02:48,082 --> 00:02:52,504
[SPEAKER_01]: The Buddha said himself, like, sight, sound, smell, taste, touch is agreeable and disagreeable.

35
00:02:53,605 --> 00:02:57,687
[SPEAKER_01]: They're besetting, they're attacking your senses.

36
00:02:59,398 --> 00:03:02,139
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what sides do, so to speak.

37
00:03:02,439 --> 00:03:06,640
[SPEAKER_01]: So you realize that it's your own senses that that's where the problem is.

38
00:03:07,221 --> 00:03:19,665
[SPEAKER_01]: But for as long as you haven't been withdrawn from the sense object, if you haven't stopped acting towards the person that upset you, acting out, you will be maintaining the notion that that's where the problem is.

39
00:03:20,065 --> 00:03:21,966
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's exactly the root misconceiving.

40
00:03:22,226 --> 00:03:25,347
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, you don't see your body for what it is.

41
00:03:25,627 --> 00:03:28,708
[SPEAKER_01]: These sense organs that actually you resist.

42
00:03:29,665 --> 00:03:36,006
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why you delight in sense-objects of agreeable kind, and that's why you reverse to the sense-objects of disagreeable kind.

43
00:03:36,766 --> 00:03:39,767
[SPEAKER_01]: Because, fundamentally, you don't want to have to deal.

44
00:03:40,667 --> 00:03:50,009
[SPEAKER_01]: You don't want to face that voidness of those sense-organs, the lack of substance, because it reveals non-ownership.

45
00:03:50,929 --> 00:03:56,010
[SPEAKER_01]: If you were to see the eye, truly, for what it is, as a sense-base because of which there are sights,

46
00:03:57,998 --> 00:04:00,700
[SPEAKER_01]: You realize it's inaccessible to you.

47
00:04:00,740 --> 00:04:10,348
[SPEAKER_01]: Any sense of control you had, preferences for pleasing, avoiding displeasing sides, all that was completely circumstantial on the basis you are fully trapped within it.

48
00:04:11,469 --> 00:04:12,850
[SPEAKER_01]: And exactly there is no outside of it.

49
00:04:13,551 --> 00:04:15,533
[SPEAKER_01]: What you see is your eye seeing.

50
00:04:17,547 --> 00:04:29,811
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you develop this notion, the knowledge of the world outside, because of which you feel like you freed yourself from these pressure of these five senses, five sense organs, the body.

51
00:04:30,071 --> 00:04:31,051
[SPEAKER_01]: But that's the wrong notion.

52
00:04:31,231 --> 00:04:40,594
[SPEAKER_01]: And for as long as you maintain that wrong notion, you're never going to take on that pressure correctly, and you will not be able to free yourself from it.

53
00:04:43,195 --> 00:04:46,196
[SPEAKER_00]: So, your senses are sort of open for attack.

54
00:04:47,770 --> 00:04:51,212
[SPEAKER_00]: And you can't... how do you protect that?

55
00:04:51,352 --> 00:04:52,592
[SPEAKER_01]: It's like... that's what I mean.

56
00:04:52,612 --> 00:04:54,753
[SPEAKER_01]: They're completely inaccessible to you.

57
00:04:55,353 --> 00:05:00,335
[SPEAKER_01]: You can't... you don't even have a say in how senses see things or hear things.

58
00:05:00,976 --> 00:05:02,056
[SPEAKER_01]: You only get the result of it.

59
00:05:06,318 --> 00:05:17,306
[SPEAKER_01]: For as long as you, as I said, don't sufficiently withdraw yourself from sense objects, you will entertain a degree of notion of control over sense objects, because senses don't appear.

60
00:05:17,886 --> 00:05:19,548
[SPEAKER_01]: These sense bases, you can't see them.

61
00:05:19,668 --> 00:05:21,389
[SPEAKER_01]: Eye cannot see itself, ear cannot hear itself.

62
00:05:21,849 --> 00:05:25,432
[SPEAKER_01]: So it's negative, hollow, empty, all those things that the suttas describe them with.

63
00:05:26,333 --> 00:05:30,656
[SPEAKER_01]: And because of that, all you see is you and me, and this anger.

64
00:05:32,285 --> 00:05:39,793
[SPEAKER_01]: Or, whatever, this pleasing thing in me, and this pleasure, so it's for me, it's mine, I want it, I don't want it.

65
00:05:40,273 --> 00:05:47,581
[SPEAKER_01]: But you are completely outside of that whole relationship between that I that's being harassed and besetted by these sights, and so on.

66
00:05:50,384 --> 00:05:53,187
[SPEAKER_01]: But for as long as you don't withdraw yourself from Saitam's Maltese touches,

67
00:05:54,342 --> 00:06:00,486
[SPEAKER_01]: You will not see that there is something else there, that doesn't appear on that level, that background of pressuring body for what it is.

68
00:06:00,967 --> 00:06:05,290
[SPEAKER_01]: What I was describing, the natural patīgā that you discover, it's like, oh, that's where it is.

69
00:06:06,050 --> 00:06:08,052
[SPEAKER_00]: So would you say that you can perceive them?

70
00:06:08,692 --> 00:06:09,853
[SPEAKER_01]: Can you perceive the senses?

71
00:06:09,913 --> 00:06:10,053
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

72
00:06:10,233 --> 00:06:10,874
[SPEAKER_01]: You can know them.

73
00:06:11,034 --> 00:06:17,959
[SPEAKER_01]: You get to... By not misconceiving the perception on account of them, you get to understand the nature of perception.

74
00:06:17,999 --> 00:06:23,303
[SPEAKER_01]: In other words, you get to understand the nature of those hollow negative senses, devoid of substance.

75
00:06:24,143 --> 00:06:25,343
[SPEAKER_00]: That you cannot perceive.

76
00:06:25,543 --> 00:06:26,464
[SPEAKER_01]: You cannot see directly.

77
00:06:26,484 --> 00:06:36,466
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why that whole point of discerning the peripheral context and everything else, because if you expect you're gonna see a nimitta of what your eyes are, that's, again, that's not gonna be nowhere near.

78
00:06:37,947 --> 00:06:43,048
[SPEAKER_01]: And they would have said that if a man were to examine those those sense bases and he compared them to those empty rooms.

79
00:06:44,106 --> 00:06:45,146
[SPEAKER_01]: Like a man... empty village.

80
00:06:45,686 --> 00:06:49,307
[SPEAKER_01]: The man escapes the vipers and so on, and comes to an empty village.

81
00:06:49,988 --> 00:06:51,628
[SPEAKER_01]: And he's just devoid of anybody.

82
00:06:51,648 --> 00:06:52,688
[SPEAKER_01]: He's just empty and hollow.

83
00:06:52,828 --> 00:06:54,089
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's what the senses are.

84
00:06:54,449 --> 00:06:56,549
[SPEAKER_01]: They're just devoid of presence.

85
00:06:56,889 --> 00:06:59,610
[SPEAKER_01]: And you realize, oh, this is already abandoned.

86
00:07:00,050 --> 00:07:01,011
[SPEAKER_01]: This cannot be owned.

87
00:07:01,911 --> 00:07:04,031
[SPEAKER_01]: That's already the nature of your sense bases.

88
00:07:05,452 --> 00:07:12,254
[SPEAKER_01]: But most people wouldn't even get near that to see it, because most people would not be sufficiently withdrawn from the sense objects.

89
00:07:12,534 --> 00:07:13,514
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's where the problem is.

90
00:07:15,102 --> 00:07:20,725
[SPEAKER_01]: It keeps you basically external to yourself, the assumption, by being engaged with the sense objects.

91
00:07:20,765 --> 00:07:23,206
[SPEAKER_01]: Not necessarily even just through core sensuality, in general.

92
00:07:23,806 --> 00:07:25,867
[SPEAKER_01]: The view is that, oh, you are outside.

93
00:07:26,848 --> 00:07:27,868
[SPEAKER_01]: You can get outside.

94
00:07:28,348 --> 00:07:29,929
[SPEAKER_01]: You can choose and do things outside.

95
00:07:30,649 --> 00:07:36,412
[SPEAKER_01]: But actually, all you can do is engage with your senses that see things, hear things, smell things, and so on.

96
00:07:36,432 --> 00:07:37,853
[SPEAKER_01]: There is no outside of this body.

97
00:07:37,933 --> 00:07:42,215
[SPEAKER_00]: So, this notion of myself, my identity,

98
00:07:44,505 --> 00:07:50,552
[SPEAKER_00]: That thought is in, is here, in this section of perception, this area.

99
00:07:52,113 --> 00:07:56,698
[SPEAKER_00]: And where, where's the body, where's the senses, which I am identified with?

100
00:07:57,639 --> 00:07:59,281
[SPEAKER_00]: I can't contact those things.

101
00:08:00,422 --> 00:08:00,823
[SPEAKER_01]: No, no.

102
00:08:01,043 --> 00:08:03,866
[SPEAKER_01]: Everything, everything is the result of having them already.

103
00:08:05,207 --> 00:08:05,587
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what I mean.

104
00:08:05,607 --> 00:08:12,333
[SPEAKER_01]: You can never step outside and take the ownership or protect them or choose what... You can only tame them or follow where they want to take you.

105
00:08:12,654 --> 00:08:13,014
[SPEAKER_01]: There's no...

106
00:08:13,054 --> 00:08:17,138
[SPEAKER_01]: Absolutely, there's no third alternative that you can do, because it's all that on that internal level.

107
00:08:18,461 --> 00:08:28,144
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the first thing you need to do is stop misconceiving those senses that undermine you as, as, oh, yes, yes, this is my eye and this is my ear.

108
00:08:28,164 --> 00:08:36,486
[SPEAKER_01]: Basically, you're misconceiving them through the external means and criteria that you developed on account of already misconceiving them.

109
00:08:37,138 --> 00:08:43,961
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why you develop this perception of external world and sense of control and ownership and delight and sensuality.

110
00:08:44,421 --> 00:08:46,782
[SPEAKER_01]: It's because you're already misconceiving the senses for what they are.

111
00:08:47,242 --> 00:08:52,484
[SPEAKER_01]: Now, on account of that misconceiving, you develop the view about external world through which now you think you can access these senses.

112
00:08:52,524 --> 00:08:54,825
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's like a double, sort of, misconceiving.

113
00:08:57,006 --> 00:09:00,587
[SPEAKER_01]: And when people look like, oh, yes, this, the eye is just this medical thing and stuff.

114
00:09:00,627 --> 00:09:01,588
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, when you look at it.

115
00:09:02,440 --> 00:09:05,563
[SPEAKER_01]: Not as that because of which there is looking personally.

116
00:09:05,603 --> 00:09:11,328
[SPEAKER_01]: You can never see internally eye the same way you're dissecting it in a lab or something.

117
00:09:11,908 --> 00:09:18,594
[SPEAKER_01]: That's an object that I can see because of these eyes that are not object, not on the level of the object.

118
00:09:18,614 --> 00:09:23,398
[SPEAKER_01]: Because if these eyes become on the level of the object, I will not have my sight anymore.

119
00:09:27,837 --> 00:09:34,521
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you can look at them, you know, as a doctor, scientist can look at an eye and see how it works.

120
00:09:35,141 --> 00:09:46,387
[SPEAKER_01]: But you need to see that that... you are accessing that through your own eyes already, which means it can never be that internal counterpart, that sense base that's always internally.

121
00:09:47,367 --> 00:09:48,888
[SPEAKER_00]: So, how do you know that it's there?

122
00:09:49,548 --> 00:09:50,609
[SPEAKER_01]: How do you know that it's there?

123
00:09:50,829 --> 00:09:55,912
[SPEAKER_01]: By withdrawing yourself from satsangs, malte sthācchas that otherwise please you or displease you, by not acting towards them.

124
00:09:55,932 --> 00:09:56,753
[SPEAKER_01]: Then, what do you find?

125
00:09:57,133 --> 00:09:59,534
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, you find that empty hollow space.

126
00:09:59,994 --> 00:10:02,016
[SPEAKER_01]: You find that empty village that the Buddha talks about.

127
00:10:02,736 --> 00:10:13,162
[SPEAKER_01]: You realize, yeah, this hollowness is that body because of which I was confusing myself to be the conceiver and perceiver and owner and master of the world.

128
00:10:14,125 --> 00:10:22,750
[SPEAKER_01]: Yet, it's because of that, this absolutely unownable, empty, abandoned village that everything has fled from, because it's subject to ruin.

129
00:10:25,311 --> 00:10:34,716
[SPEAKER_01]: So, then, you will not entertain the notion that you are the perceiver and conceiver of the world, because you just saw that notion being completely undermined and dismantled.

130
00:10:36,257 --> 00:10:37,818
[SPEAKER_01]: And there is a sutra which understands that.

131
00:10:37,898 --> 00:10:41,520
[SPEAKER_01]: It's because of that, that one is the perceiver and conceiver of the world.

132
00:10:42,955 --> 00:10:44,236
[SPEAKER_01]: Because he doesn't understand the I.

133
00:10:44,917 --> 00:10:48,279
[SPEAKER_01]: So, he becomes... yeah, I see this, I perceive this, I conceive this.

134
00:10:49,100 --> 00:10:52,483
[SPEAKER_01]: Because, as I said, there's nothing else that appears there in those palpable terms.

135
00:10:53,163 --> 00:10:58,768
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's why a person needs to develop internally to recognize these negative counterparts as necessary basis.

136
00:10:58,788 --> 00:11:04,452
[SPEAKER_01]: But, practically speaking, what you're going to find is just this unity of your body experienced internally

137
00:11:06,994 --> 00:11:20,317
[SPEAKER_01]: whereby the the external thoughts that you might have in regard to that body, in regard to the eye and ear, are seen second to the internal experience of the body internally as a hollow empty vessel.

138
00:11:20,337 --> 00:11:23,198
[SPEAKER_00]: You're saying the thoughts are actually seen as external.

139
00:11:23,258 --> 00:11:28,002
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, you cannot get rid of the thought, so I shall not, I must not think the I, if I try to see the I.

140
00:11:28,042 --> 00:11:39,632
[SPEAKER_01]: You will think the I, but you should not conceive your thought of the I, to be that I, that is internally there, as that negative, hollow, empty vessel, empty room, empty village.

141
00:11:41,453 --> 00:11:51,021
[SPEAKER_01]: So, training in regard to that internal negative space, for the lack of better word, will then unpervert the order

142
00:11:51,949 --> 00:11:56,991
[SPEAKER_01]: ...of your thoughts in regard to the I and that which the I-base actually is.

143
00:11:57,031 --> 00:11:58,551
[SPEAKER_01]: It will remove the base for conceiving.

144
00:11:59,571 --> 00:12:01,612
[SPEAKER_01]: Then, yes, you will have the thoughts about the I's.

145
00:12:01,672 --> 00:12:02,592
[SPEAKER_01]: They were never the problem.

146
00:12:03,253 --> 00:12:11,575
[SPEAKER_01]: But you will not carry... they will not carry the assumption that, yes, those thoughts which are basically external, and about external things, are my I's.

147
00:12:12,696 --> 00:12:20,018
[SPEAKER_01]: Now, I's are that internal, hollow, unownable, subject to ruin, village that everybody has fled... fled from.

148
00:12:21,770 --> 00:12:22,371
[SPEAKER_01]: That's your body.

149
00:12:22,411 --> 00:12:23,251
[SPEAKER_01]: Those are your senses.

150
00:12:24,892 --> 00:12:29,354
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if you're able to see that way, the conceivings will fade away.

151
00:12:30,455 --> 00:12:40,140
[SPEAKER_01]: You will not have to then make the effort to stop conceiving or misconceiving, because you realize, oh no, this is subject to, you know, flooding and attacks and stuff.

152
00:12:40,220 --> 00:12:41,241
[SPEAKER_01]: I better not be there.

153
00:12:42,917 --> 00:12:44,138
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's how you free yourself from it.

154
00:12:44,298 --> 00:12:47,680
[SPEAKER_01]: You can't free yourself from it by pulling your eyes out.

155
00:12:47,760 --> 00:13:05,231
[SPEAKER_01]: You can free yourself by completely removing any misconceived notion of ownership in regard to the sights and the eyes and both and everything else in between that used to exist, being stuff you felt on account of sights, sounds, smells, tastes, touches, acts, things you did, choices you made, intentions, thoughts you had.

156
00:13:05,651 --> 00:13:08,012
[SPEAKER_01]: All of that's on the result of that basis.

157
00:13:11,947 --> 00:13:13,928
[SPEAKER_00]: We had another question about memories.

158
00:13:14,629 --> 00:13:18,791
[SPEAKER_00]: Where are memories stored, you know?

159
00:13:18,851 --> 00:13:20,752
[SPEAKER_00]: Where's the memory of yesterday and the day before?

160
00:13:21,472 --> 00:13:21,913
[SPEAKER_00]: Where is that?

161
00:13:21,973 --> 00:13:26,375
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, at the same place where the thoughts and images of that question come from.

162
00:13:28,026 --> 00:13:29,787
[SPEAKER_01]: So, where the memory is stored?

163
00:13:29,927 --> 00:13:32,849
[SPEAKER_01]: Where are these designations that I'm using to ask you a question?

164
00:13:32,969 --> 00:13:33,830
[SPEAKER_01]: Where is that stored?

165
00:13:34,591 --> 00:13:37,593
[SPEAKER_01]: And then you realize it's not... it's kind of an invalid question.

166
00:13:38,073 --> 00:13:46,639
[SPEAKER_01]: Because it assumes an external point of view that can see the storage of my, basically, consciousness and thoughts and everything else.

167
00:13:47,179 --> 00:13:48,580
[SPEAKER_01]: And you cannot conceive that.

168
00:13:48,700 --> 00:13:50,662
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, you can misconceive that, as I said.

169
00:13:51,422 --> 00:13:54,765
[SPEAKER_01]: Assuming the outside of yourself is only, like, basically

170
00:13:56,085 --> 00:13:57,746
[SPEAKER_01]: Can only be a form of misconceiving.

171
00:13:57,946 --> 00:14:05,090
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the notion of external, storage or whatever else, it's very much on the basis of your internal that comes first.

172
00:14:05,890 --> 00:14:06,591
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's the point.

173
00:14:07,331 --> 00:14:08,852
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you can have those thoughts.

174
00:14:09,947 --> 00:14:11,127
[SPEAKER_01]: So, I must stop thinking this.

175
00:14:11,328 --> 00:14:13,268
[SPEAKER_01]: But you must stop misconceiving the order.

176
00:14:13,308 --> 00:14:22,832
[SPEAKER_01]: You must stop putting the thought of external first, the thought in regard to the external sense object first, the meditation techniques about sense objects and nimittas and visions.

177
00:14:23,272 --> 00:14:33,656
[SPEAKER_01]: Stop putting that first and start discerning that negative, basically empty, abandoned sense organ, body as internal, as that basis.

178
00:14:34,317 --> 00:14:35,537
[SPEAKER_01]: That is what you're bound with.

179
00:14:35,957 --> 00:14:37,078
[SPEAKER_01]: There is no outside of it.

180
00:14:38,205 --> 00:14:45,386
[SPEAKER_01]: All the external perceptions, and notions, and designations, and thoughts, and questions you might have, is within that internal body you are bound with.

181
00:14:46,567 --> 00:14:50,407
[SPEAKER_00]: But then...

182
00:14:50,427 --> 00:15:00,989
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the point is not to really figure out, get information, or try and find, you know, get hold of the eye, get hold of the ears, and really understand how they work...

183
00:15:01,009 --> 00:15:04,330
[SPEAKER_01]: But people would still hold the view that they can, and that it's about that.

184
00:15:05,390 --> 00:15:11,121
[SPEAKER_01]: But, that's why it will never... you're only gonna basically get frustrated and you will not find the answer.

185
00:15:11,201 --> 00:15:13,406
[SPEAKER_01]: Because, yeah, it's based on the wrong premise.

186
00:15:15,675 --> 00:15:21,837
[SPEAKER_00]: There is the mind, there is mind-objects, and there's mind-consciousness, and then the coming together of the three is context.

187
00:15:21,857 --> 00:15:28,198
[SPEAKER_00]: So, how does it come together, and why does it come together, and where is the mind, where is the objects exactly situated, where is the consciousness?

188
00:15:28,898 --> 00:15:33,739
[SPEAKER_00]: But that's... but you can't... to try and figure that out, you can come up with some fancy ideas.

189
00:15:34,740 --> 00:15:36,280
[SPEAKER_00]: But that's not... not the point.

190
00:15:36,420 --> 00:15:38,881
[SPEAKER_00]: That description seems to me to be enough.

191
00:15:40,181 --> 00:15:40,441
[SPEAKER_01]: It is.

192
00:15:40,502 --> 00:15:44,805
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not, it's, it's, it's, it's not about figuring out the relationship of those things.

193
00:15:45,026 --> 00:15:49,570
[SPEAKER_01]: It's about just not falling into the trap of misconceiving and becoming the owner of it.

194
00:15:50,090 --> 00:15:54,554
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why the, all the interpretations of that description came later, did not come from the Buddha.

195
00:15:55,455 --> 00:16:00,420
[SPEAKER_01]: You know, what, how that meeting occurs, like slapping of the hands and the sound is the result.

196
00:16:00,540 --> 00:16:01,681
[SPEAKER_01]: That's not from the suttas.

197
00:16:02,742 --> 00:16:05,945
[SPEAKER_01]: It's literally there in the world, the hollow

198
00:16:06,522 --> 00:16:12,751
[SPEAKER_01]: village that gets attacked every now and then, and the result of that attack is basically the pressure that you can feel...

199
00:16:13,751 --> 00:16:18,393
[SPEAKER_01]: On account of seeing, smelling, tasting, touching, that's agreeable, disagreeable, it's pulling you in the directions.

200
00:16:19,113 --> 00:16:20,533
[SPEAKER_01]: How it happens, it's irrelevant.

201
00:16:20,914 --> 00:16:23,935
[SPEAKER_01]: Because the fact is that you run... that you cannot remain unmoved.

202
00:16:24,095 --> 00:16:24,855
[SPEAKER_01]: That's your problem.

203
00:16:25,135 --> 00:16:26,676
[SPEAKER_01]: Contact has to cease.

204
00:16:27,256 --> 00:16:32,678
[SPEAKER_01]: Not by removing the village or that which comes into village to attack it, but by removing your bother by it.

205
00:16:33,318 --> 00:16:41,581
[SPEAKER_01]: So that's where the only way to know the eye, to know the object correctly, is first to see that you can only know them on the basis of pressure already being there.

206
00:16:42,141 --> 00:16:45,163
[SPEAKER_00]: You're a secondary, in a kind of secondary place.

207
00:16:45,183 --> 00:16:46,783
[SPEAKER_00]: You have no access to those things.

208
00:16:46,903 --> 00:16:47,284
[SPEAKER_00]: No, no.

209
00:16:47,424 --> 00:16:48,304
[SPEAKER_00]: Control or anything.

210
00:16:48,484 --> 00:17:02,151
[SPEAKER_01]: And then pressure is the measure of, you know, whether you understood it or not, whether you're trying to get rid of it through finding answers, or you're able to endure it and see through it and then remove, basically, that patīgā towards that internal aspect.

211
00:17:02,911 --> 00:17:05,713
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, whatever comes, it will just come through, so to speak.

212
00:17:06,533 --> 00:17:07,894
[SPEAKER_01]: You will not be bothered by it.

213
00:17:09,021 --> 00:17:22,588
[SPEAKER_01]: But if people already have the view, and most of them would, of that external explanatory, oh, this is what happens, as that, as if that's relevant to the fact that you're pressured by the pleasing and pressured by the displeasing, that's the, if that's the core, that's the meeting spot.

214
00:17:23,629 --> 00:17:30,432
[SPEAKER_01]: And now you're gonna go and solve out how this meeting happens by abandoning the meeting spot and investigating sort of theoretical aspects of it.

215
00:17:30,472 --> 00:17:30,592
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

216
00:17:31,153 --> 00:17:35,195
[SPEAKER_01]: The only way to solve, to undo the contact, is to endure it through where it is.

217
00:17:37,040 --> 00:17:51,609
[SPEAKER_01]: And even like the prerequisite for the right view was the Buddha said to restrain yourself from falling into seeking answers for who am I, what was, was I in the past, will I be in the future, all these external answers that pertain to the core of your sense of self.

218
00:17:51,989 --> 00:17:58,273
[SPEAKER_01]: Because that takes the sense of self for granted and it also assumes it externally by thinking I can find the answers for it externally.

219
00:17:59,274 --> 00:18:03,757
[SPEAKER_01]: And if a person needs to recognize, yes, sense of self is a problem, it's the root of suffering and so on,

220
00:18:04,290 --> 00:18:08,031
[SPEAKER_01]: But, I must refrain myself from seeking these questions out there.

221
00:18:08,171 --> 00:18:17,414
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if you refrain... that pressure to find these answers, which is always rooted in trying to get rid of the pressure, by the way.

222
00:18:17,814 --> 00:18:25,276
[SPEAKER_01]: But, if you refrain from seeking these external answers, and stay with the problem on that internal level, that's the... that's pretty much the first step.

223
00:18:25,356 --> 00:18:26,256
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the correct step.

224
00:18:26,837 --> 00:18:28,617
[SPEAKER_01]: That's where sense restraint always comes first.

225
00:18:28,697 --> 00:18:31,618
[SPEAKER_01]: And, you know, as we spoke before, like, if somebody, something upsets you,

226
00:18:32,788 --> 00:18:39,413
[SPEAKER_01]: You have to stop acting towards that thing, because otherwise you will never see that that thing was never the root of your upset.

227
00:18:39,573 --> 00:18:42,796
[SPEAKER_01]: It was your internal craving, in regard to what you internally felt.

228
00:18:43,716 --> 00:18:58,168
[SPEAKER_01]: In regard to the internal base, that has perceived something externally, which is within the internal base, because you cannot actually have something externally, independent... independently accessed or perceived, independently of the... your sense organ.

229
00:18:58,788 --> 00:19:01,950
[SPEAKER_01]: So, all you can perceive is sense organs seeing or hearing or smelling or touching.

230
00:19:02,010 --> 00:19:02,970
[SPEAKER_01]: So, there's no outside of it.

231
00:19:04,251 --> 00:19:08,853
[SPEAKER_01]: There is no outside of it means already there is no assumption of me being outside and accessing outside.

232
00:19:08,933 --> 00:19:11,375
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's already shrinking of attavāda and so on.

233
00:19:12,363 --> 00:19:13,184
[SPEAKER_01]: But that takes effort.

234
00:19:13,204 --> 00:19:14,725
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not about finding the answer.

235
00:19:15,346 --> 00:19:26,856
[SPEAKER_01]: It's about actually enduring that pressure to seek and resolve the issue of myself, and what I am, and who I am, and where it came from, or the issue of the contact, to resolve it on that external plane.

236
00:19:27,577 --> 00:19:32,742
[SPEAKER_01]: Because that's already a perverted order, and you're looking at the wrong place, and feeding the perversion of the order.

237
00:19:34,000 --> 00:19:41,123
[SPEAKER_00]: So, if you become then mindful of the body, in this way, where you... Internally.

238
00:19:41,303 --> 00:19:44,965
[SPEAKER_00]: You understand, you don't have access to the body.

239
00:19:45,145 --> 00:19:56,130
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you can become mindful of the body internally, by not falling into a trap of putting the thoughts of your body as that which your body is.

240
00:19:57,711 --> 00:20:01,513
[SPEAKER_01]: So, when I say be mindful of the body, the first thing you want to have is an image of your body.

241
00:20:02,786 --> 00:20:03,266
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's fine.

242
00:20:03,787 --> 00:20:07,871
[SPEAKER_01]: But through that image of the body, there is the internal physicality of that body being there.

243
00:20:08,471 --> 00:20:09,572
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the base of mindfulness.

244
00:20:09,672 --> 00:20:11,134
[SPEAKER_01]: Seeing body within the body.

245
00:20:12,114 --> 00:20:22,224
[SPEAKER_01]: But the problem is that people expect some magical result out of it, and then they fail to look at that... fail to see that the actual problem is... it's just that.

246
00:20:22,604 --> 00:20:23,605
[SPEAKER_01]: It's just what you put first.

247
00:20:23,925 --> 00:20:24,626
[SPEAKER_01]: Nothing else there.

248
00:20:25,480 --> 00:20:29,464
[SPEAKER_01]: Do you put that physicality of the body... See, even physicality of the body is a form of thought.

249
00:20:30,324 --> 00:20:32,626
[SPEAKER_01]: And that can become a form of misconceiving then.

250
00:20:32,726 --> 00:20:33,967
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the Mūla Pāryāya Sutta.

251
00:20:34,708 --> 00:20:36,910
[SPEAKER_01]: You misconceive the form, one way or the other.

252
00:20:37,971 --> 00:20:39,212
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's where the practice is.

253
00:20:39,853 --> 00:20:40,974
[SPEAKER_01]: You recognize the thought,

254
00:20:41,767 --> 00:20:47,951
[SPEAKER_01]: You don't take it for granted as, oh, that's what my body is, because it is an external thought in regard to that physicality.

255
00:20:48,812 --> 00:21:03,762
[SPEAKER_01]: Through the enduring of the thought, through the enduring of that contact, pressure, you... you develop yourself to that counterpart of physicality that is there, because of which you wouldn't, you know, otherwise you wouldn't even have that thought there.

256
00:21:03,782 --> 00:21:05,483
[SPEAKER_01]: So, mindfulness of the body, fine.

257
00:21:05,984 --> 00:21:07,765
[SPEAKER_01]: Even have a thought of your posture or whatever.

258
00:21:08,525 --> 00:21:10,267
[SPEAKER_01]: If you just sit down, mindfully,

259
00:21:11,150 --> 00:21:12,831
[SPEAKER_01]: You are already aware that you're seated.

260
00:21:12,991 --> 00:21:14,351
[SPEAKER_01]: That's already an image in your mind.

261
00:21:14,471 --> 00:21:14,991
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's fine.

262
00:21:16,012 --> 00:21:20,593
[SPEAKER_01]: Through that image now, discern the more actual physicality of the seated body.

263
00:21:21,593 --> 00:21:31,657
[SPEAKER_01]: Without, again, perverting the order by allowing new thoughts to just take you into assumption that, oh, yeah, see, that's what's happening because of which this body is here.

264
00:21:32,117 --> 00:21:32,237
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

265
00:21:32,437 --> 00:21:33,957
[SPEAKER_01]: This body is here because this body is here.

266
00:21:34,438 --> 00:21:36,998
[SPEAKER_01]: Every thought you have in regard to it is within it.

267
00:21:37,079 --> 00:21:38,199
[SPEAKER_01]: Not other way around.

268
00:21:39,213 --> 00:21:42,814
[SPEAKER_01]: And that was the also like the problem with like sensation watching in meditation.

269
00:21:43,574 --> 00:21:51,637
[SPEAKER_01]: Sensation is ultimately an external point of view that you keep applying to your body with the assumption that that's what's internally felt.

270
00:21:52,217 --> 00:21:52,697
[SPEAKER_01]: But it's not.

271
00:21:52,817 --> 00:21:54,058
[SPEAKER_01]: That's touch.

272
00:21:54,118 --> 00:21:55,198
[SPEAKER_01]: It's a sense of touch, sure.

273
00:21:55,498 --> 00:21:58,559
[SPEAKER_01]: So it's not no problem like, oh, I feel sensation in my back or something.

274
00:21:59,439 --> 00:22:00,420
[SPEAKER_01]: But it's an external.

275
00:22:01,080 --> 00:22:02,800
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm being touched there, basically.

276
00:22:03,461 --> 00:22:07,542
[SPEAKER_01]: Even if it's inside of the body, that's not the ājāta, internal aspect.

277
00:22:08,623 --> 00:22:13,666
[SPEAKER_01]: which is on the level of the organ, body, as an organ that can be touched.

278
00:22:14,346 --> 00:22:16,087
[SPEAKER_01]: And that cannot be measured by sensations.

279
00:22:16,247 --> 00:22:18,208
[SPEAKER_01]: That is a negative, hollow, empty village.

280
00:22:19,269 --> 00:22:29,774
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if people have a view that sensations measure the presence of the body and the mindfulness of the body, they're basically using sense objects to measure the presence of their organ, which is impossible, which is already a form of misconceiving.

281
00:22:29,794 --> 00:22:33,536
[SPEAKER_01]: Because that's exactly why people don't see their organs, because they put the sense objects first.

282
00:22:35,879 --> 00:22:38,142
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's why no one's mindful of the body then.

283
00:22:38,182 --> 00:22:44,731
[SPEAKER_01]: No, but you... because then when you look for the body, you expect to find it on the level of sense objects, because that's what your view tells you it is there.

284
00:22:45,542 --> 00:22:50,825
[SPEAKER_01]: And then you might be refining your sense objects, refining the perceptions of touch into these subtle sensations.

285
00:22:50,865 --> 00:22:51,805
[SPEAKER_01]: That's still external.

286
00:22:51,865 --> 00:22:53,406
[SPEAKER_01]: That will always remain external.

287
00:22:54,106 --> 00:22:55,947
[SPEAKER_01]: And it's not a problem to have those things.

288
00:22:56,047 --> 00:23:06,613
[SPEAKER_01]: The problem is that you put that first, and the actual physicality of the body that is the container of the most refined sensations you must have, you might have, is actually first, and you don't see it as first.

289
00:23:06,813 --> 00:23:08,594
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, you might... you probably don't even see it at all.

290
00:23:09,074 --> 00:23:10,555
[SPEAKER_01]: If you see it, you see it as second.

291
00:23:11,575 --> 00:23:12,836
[SPEAKER_01]: You experience it as second.

292
00:23:12,876 --> 00:23:14,257
[SPEAKER_00]: But then, what you...

293
00:23:16,649 --> 00:23:33,815
[SPEAKER_00]: What you would think that internal body is then, if you haven't experienced it, you can only... you only think of it as a perception of something, an experience, which means... if I experience it, means I perceive it on some level.

294
00:23:33,955 --> 00:23:34,135
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes.

295
00:23:34,335 --> 00:23:35,235
[SPEAKER_00]: But it's not a perception.

296
00:23:35,756 --> 00:23:35,916
[SPEAKER_00]: So...

297
00:23:36,196 --> 00:23:38,757
[SPEAKER_01]: But see, saying I can't perceive it is another perception.

298
00:23:39,057 --> 00:23:40,577
[SPEAKER_01]: So you cannot not perceive it either.

299
00:23:40,997 --> 00:23:44,919
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why the whole point of Mūla Parīyāsūtra is not to not have thoughts in regard to the body,

300
00:23:45,599 --> 00:23:47,461
[SPEAKER_01]: If you do this practice, you can't expect something.

301
00:23:47,481 --> 00:23:48,061
[SPEAKER_01]: You can't have an idea.

302
00:24:13,096 --> 00:24:15,759
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, you might be expecting something, but don't put that first.

303
00:24:17,200 --> 00:24:23,927
[SPEAKER_01]: Leave it second on account of the physicality that you're doing internally, that is hollow, empty, unownable, subject to peril.

304
00:24:24,568 --> 00:24:31,936
[SPEAKER_01]: And if that's... if you're seeing your own basis like that, you will lose passion towards any prospects and objects that are kind of existing within it.

305
00:24:32,436 --> 00:24:35,680
[SPEAKER_00]: So keep seeing the thoughts of the body as secondary.

306
00:24:36,836 --> 00:24:37,016
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes.

307
00:24:37,277 --> 00:24:41,603
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, when you say, okay, the thought of the body is second, this body is first, you recognize that's a thought.

308
00:24:42,243 --> 00:24:42,604
[SPEAKER_01]: Fine.

309
00:24:42,804 --> 00:24:43,545
[SPEAKER_01]: Let it endure.

310
00:24:43,665 --> 00:24:49,353
[SPEAKER_01]: And through that, learn how to discern the physicality of that body without making it into a new object, a new thought.

311
00:24:50,214 --> 00:24:54,140
[SPEAKER_01]: That's that peripheral awareness we keep talking about, that you can infinitely practice.

312
00:24:55,371 --> 00:24:59,433
[SPEAKER_01]: And all it does, it's not take you to some special place at the end of the peripheral planes.

313
00:24:59,873 --> 00:25:00,013
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

314
00:25:00,634 --> 00:25:06,477
[SPEAKER_01]: All it does is eventually eradicates your casual ignorant habit of perverting the order.

315
00:25:06,597 --> 00:25:06,937
[SPEAKER_01]: That's it.

316
00:25:07,417 --> 00:25:14,181
[SPEAKER_01]: If you stay sufficiently on the extent necessary of that peripheral step in a way correctly,

317
00:25:15,577 --> 00:25:19,664
[SPEAKER_01]: Any tendency to flip back the order into the wrong way, will be eradicated.

318
00:25:19,724 --> 00:25:29,159
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, which will, like, as the Buddha said in Satipaṭṭhāna Sutta, or they simply practice mindfulness of the body to the extent necessary for the final knowledge to become established.

319
00:25:29,239 --> 00:25:29,620
[SPEAKER_01]: That's all.

320
00:25:30,943 --> 00:25:37,246
[SPEAKER_01]: And yeah, it's a very, like, you know, it's lots of information, theoretical and so on, but listen, re-listen, it's a very practical thing.

321
00:25:37,866 --> 00:25:47,750
[SPEAKER_01]: First, you need to be thoroughly restrained in terms of your actions, by body, by speech, by mind, because each time you act out of greed, aversion or distraction, you, you pervert the order.

322
00:25:48,190 --> 00:25:50,311
[SPEAKER_01]: You reinforce already perverted order.

323
00:25:50,331 --> 00:25:50,871
[SPEAKER_01]: You feed it.

324
00:25:50,911 --> 00:25:52,912
[SPEAKER_01]: You keep throwing fuel on that burning fire.

325
00:25:53,732 --> 00:25:57,734
[SPEAKER_01]: You stop acting, you guard your sense doors, and then you're gonna start discerning that

326
00:25:59,958 --> 00:26:04,581
[SPEAKER_01]: Negative, empty, hollow, emptiness, village, emptiness, sunyata, this is empty.

327
00:26:05,362 --> 00:26:11,526
[SPEAKER_01]: And you will not necessarily, oh, this is the eye, this is... You can just see it in the most genetic terms of the body, but you will not...

328
00:26:11,566 --> 00:26:17,310
[SPEAKER_01]: External perceptions will be seen for what they are, and that internal sense of emptiness will be then seen.

329
00:26:17,510 --> 00:26:19,892
[SPEAKER_01]: That's that sense base that I have no outside of.

330
00:26:20,292 --> 00:26:25,716
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the practical way of practicing mindfulness, once you've been thoroughly restrained,

331
00:26:26,554 --> 00:26:32,778
[SPEAKER_01]: Because if you're not, that's your practice of mindfulness, a thorough restraint, guarding of the sense door, moderation in eating, watchfulness.

332
00:26:33,279 --> 00:26:39,143
[SPEAKER_01]: Then, if you want to do more on top of that, you just do the same, but this have already gathered, so to speak.

333
00:26:39,803 --> 00:26:49,610
[SPEAKER_01]: But your sense restraint and effort into its, you know, sīla and virtue and growing on account of it, what that has gathered, you realize, okay, so now, I'm not leaking outside, I'm not spilling outside,

334
00:26:50,880 --> 00:27:00,129
[SPEAKER_01]: My behavior has been restrained, so when I have the thoughts of the body, you can actually allow it to endure, and within that, see the present physicality, because of which this thought is there.

335
00:27:01,530 --> 00:27:04,693
[SPEAKER_01]: So you can never get to the pure physicality, because that's a thought.

336
00:27:05,855 --> 00:27:11,460
[SPEAKER_01]: If you start coming to it as an object, the only way to objectify it, is through having an image of it.

337
00:27:11,520 --> 00:27:14,183
[SPEAKER_01]: Which means, physicality has been misconceived.

338
00:27:15,050 --> 00:27:29,221
[SPEAKER_01]: So, all you have to do is stop trying to access it through the assumption of access, and just see what's there, and stop putting the thoughts first, let them endure, and then discern the negative physicality underneath it.

339
00:27:30,621 --> 00:27:37,063
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's... that's pretty much, like, practice... well, that's kind of the culmination of the first jhāna, of the level of withdrawal.

340
00:27:37,583 --> 00:27:44,545
[SPEAKER_01]: But your practice of first jhāna, as we said before, starts by not acting, restraining your speech, guarding your sense doors.

341
00:27:44,765 --> 00:27:45,965
[SPEAKER_01]: You're already gathering in.

342
00:27:47,045 --> 00:27:56,908
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why in first jhāna you would have thoughts, thinking and pondering, you know, picking up the content and whatever way people translate vittāka-vicāra, but the order will remain unperverted.

343
00:27:58,104 --> 00:28:12,754
[SPEAKER_01]: If you're not established in the physicality of that body, if you have not sufficiently stopped misconceiving it, and putting it second, and putting the thoughts as more fundamental, every time you have vittaka, it comes from the outside, as that which is first.

344
00:28:12,874 --> 00:28:21,520
[SPEAKER_01]: Because each time the thought appears, unless, as I said, you have been developed to the extent necessary, it will come with at least that initial perversion of order.

345
00:28:22,857 --> 00:28:28,280
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why people who have developed jhānas in the suttas, it's said like, oh, they're able to purify the thought in its arising.

346
00:28:28,460 --> 00:28:31,802
[SPEAKER_01]: In other words, in the arising of the thought, order will remain unperverted.

347
00:28:31,922 --> 00:28:33,103
[SPEAKER_01]: There will be no pollution.

348
00:28:34,884 --> 00:28:36,465
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's sustaining that order.

349
00:28:36,645 --> 00:28:39,306
[SPEAKER_01]: And you can start sustaining that order in a broader sense.

350
00:28:40,907 --> 00:28:42,928
[SPEAKER_01]: The order of sense restraint.

351
00:28:43,148 --> 00:28:44,809
[SPEAKER_01]: The order of the aggregate of virtue.

352
00:28:45,550 --> 00:28:46,710
[SPEAKER_01]: That becomes first now.

353
00:28:47,151 --> 00:28:49,792
[SPEAKER_01]: See, virtue is not first either.

354
00:28:49,892 --> 00:28:50,973
[SPEAKER_01]: Acting out is first.

355
00:28:52,135 --> 00:29:01,397
[SPEAKER_01]: Then you pondered and you understood that you need to be restrained and now you start actually preventing yourself from putting the acts of non-virtue first, making them factual.

356
00:29:02,257 --> 00:29:14,120
[SPEAKER_01]: And if you've been cultivating virtue sufficiently enough for a period of time, you start to physically recognize an aggregate of virtue, an aggregate of certain non-behavior that you cultivated and now that's first.

357
00:29:14,840 --> 00:29:20,481
[SPEAKER_01]: And if you choose to break it, now you realize, ah, that would be perverting the order, that would be going against the right order.

358
00:29:21,773 --> 00:29:22,795
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, same with speech.

359
00:29:23,135 --> 00:29:26,800
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, eventually, you can do that on the level of thoughts, because that's where the conceivings happen.

360
00:29:28,002 --> 00:29:34,371
[SPEAKER_01]: That's where you pervert the fundamental order and put the thought, the image of your body first, not the physicality of the body.

361
00:29:35,713 --> 00:29:37,796
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's the whole, eh...

362
00:29:38,581 --> 00:29:41,722
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, yeah, the whole Mūḍha-pariyāya Sutta, how one misconceives.

363
00:29:42,162 --> 00:29:51,223
[SPEAKER_01]: But there are other suttas as well, about that, when there is a contact, say, I have a thought of the body, there is the patīgā aspect of it, and there is the adhivācana aspect of it.

364
00:29:51,603 --> 00:29:55,444
[SPEAKER_01]: There is the resistance aspect of it, and there is the designation aspect of it.

365
00:29:55,464 --> 00:29:56,844
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the core of every contact.

366
00:29:58,565 --> 00:30:01,505
[SPEAKER_01]: And, usually, it's the designation that's put first.

367
00:30:03,885 --> 00:30:04,966
[SPEAKER_01]: They're simultaneously there.

368
00:30:05,006 --> 00:30:06,526
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not that designation comes later.

369
00:30:07,434 --> 00:30:09,376
[SPEAKER_01]: So, thought of the body doesn't come later.

370
00:30:09,956 --> 00:30:13,099
[SPEAKER_01]: That thought of the body is there with the body, which is why you know it's the body.

371
00:30:13,779 --> 00:30:17,802
[SPEAKER_01]: So, thought designates that resistance, ambiguity, that patīgā.

372
00:30:18,483 --> 00:30:21,505
[SPEAKER_01]: But it cannot go outside and possess it or be separate to it.

373
00:30:21,946 --> 00:30:24,508
[SPEAKER_01]: Yet, that's what every misconceiving carries.

374
00:30:24,548 --> 00:30:28,311
[SPEAKER_01]: Implication that that's the body, already you put the body second.

375
00:30:28,551 --> 00:30:31,173
[SPEAKER_01]: And you stop seeing patīgā of the body for what it is.

376
00:30:33,655 --> 00:30:40,117
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's the resistance contact, translated in the Sutta sometimes, and the designation contact.

377
00:30:40,137 --> 00:30:41,457
[SPEAKER_01]: The two aspects of the same thing.

378
00:30:42,377 --> 00:30:45,438
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's where the perversion happens, within that pressure of contact.

379
00:30:46,058 --> 00:30:46,538
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's what I mean.

380
00:30:46,558 --> 00:30:57,701
[SPEAKER_01]: You have to stop acting, you have to be able to endure the pressure of the contact, pleasant or unpleasant, and then, within that, see the physicality of it, simultaneously present with the thought of the physicality of it.

381
00:30:58,781 --> 00:30:59,881
[SPEAKER_01]: And don't pervert that order.

382
00:31:00,081 --> 00:31:02,722
[SPEAKER_01]: Allow it to endure and keep sustaining it and protecting it.

383
00:31:04,913 --> 00:31:13,780
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, you can think freely, without any misconceivings, without any underlying tendency finding ways back, and that's basically thinking and pondering of the first jhāna.

384
00:31:14,440 --> 00:31:27,590
[SPEAKER_01]: And when the body is there, unified, how the suttas will say, the pleasure of that unification is there, that whole thing, because you're fully withdrawn, and no amount of thinking can pervert the order, and there is a sense of safety on account of it, the profound sense of safety.

385
00:31:28,050 --> 00:31:30,072
[SPEAKER_01]: Because the threat was not that there was a village,

386
00:31:31,190 --> 00:31:34,753
[SPEAKER_01]: The threat was that you didn't know how to leave it.

387
00:31:35,874 --> 00:31:37,015
[SPEAKER_01]: The threat was that you were there.

388
00:31:37,495 --> 00:31:39,177
[SPEAKER_01]: And now, you are not there anymore.

389
00:31:39,257 --> 00:31:40,218
[SPEAKER_00]: You remove the ownership.

390
00:31:40,638 --> 00:31:47,804
[SPEAKER_00]: This right order that you're speaking about, that you're speaking about now, right order, that's the right view.

391
00:31:48,564 --> 00:31:48,945
[SPEAKER_00]: The right...

392
00:31:49,025 --> 00:31:49,205
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes.

393
00:31:49,465 --> 00:31:50,286
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the right view.

394
00:31:50,326 --> 00:31:50,946
[SPEAKER_01]: That's... yeah.

395
00:31:51,246 --> 00:31:51,767
[SPEAKER_00]: And...

396
00:31:51,867 --> 00:31:56,311
[SPEAKER_01]: Without the right view of what the right order is, you will not even know what the right order is to look for.

397
00:31:56,331 --> 00:31:56,611
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

398
00:31:56,751 --> 00:31:57,231
[SPEAKER_00]: But you can...

399
00:31:57,592 --> 00:31:59,093
[SPEAKER_00]: So, if someone can get an idea of that,

400
00:31:59,839 --> 00:32:01,420
[SPEAKER_01]: Follow that idea and you will get the right view.

401
00:32:02,341 --> 00:32:03,381
[SPEAKER_00]: Or remember that idea.

402
00:32:03,881 --> 00:32:04,702
[SPEAKER_00]: Remember that idea.

403
00:32:04,722 --> 00:32:05,542
[SPEAKER_00]: Sati that idea.

404
00:32:05,703 --> 00:32:06,303
[SPEAKER_01]: Sati.

405
00:32:06,443 --> 00:32:08,024
[SPEAKER_01]: Have an accurate memory of that idea.

406
00:32:08,464 --> 00:32:09,285
[SPEAKER_00]: Keep on remembering.

407
00:32:09,505 --> 00:32:10,265
[SPEAKER_00]: Keep on remembering.

408
00:32:10,405 --> 00:32:20,051
[SPEAKER_01]: But, obviously, that idea will not have anything to pertain to and be recognized as factual, unless your behavior has provided sufficient basis for it.

409
00:32:21,270 --> 00:32:23,671
[SPEAKER_00]: So, your behavior needs to be purified beforehand.

410
00:32:23,691 --> 00:32:25,211
[SPEAKER_00]: It just remains theoretical.

411
00:32:25,631 --> 00:32:32,693
[SPEAKER_01]: It remains theoretical and pondering, but you will not see it for yourself, because there is no matching physicality of it, of the right order.

412
00:32:32,893 --> 00:32:37,454
[SPEAKER_01]: Everything you live, on a day-to-day basis, is through the perverted order.

413
00:32:37,734 --> 00:32:46,557
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you can have all the thoughts you want about the right order, unless your basic physical behavior starts to emulate the right order, there is no basis for any of that to take root.

414
00:32:48,290 --> 00:32:55,097
[SPEAKER_01]: You cannot practice the right order while you allow yourself to keep engaging in the wrong order by that which is even more fundamental than your thought.

415
00:32:55,678 --> 00:32:56,839
[SPEAKER_01]: Action by body and by speech.

416
00:32:57,600 --> 00:32:58,781
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's just not negotiable.

417
00:32:59,082 --> 00:33:01,184
[SPEAKER_01]: But you realize, actually, it's good news, as I said before.

418
00:33:01,844 --> 00:33:05,348
[SPEAKER_01]: Then, all you have to do is keep body restrained, keep your speech restrained, and you're practicing.

419
00:33:05,448 --> 00:33:08,431
[SPEAKER_01]: You're practicing the jhāna, you're practicing the right order, you're practicing towards the right view.

420
00:33:09,228 --> 00:33:12,070
[SPEAKER_01]: And then your thoughts will have much more further basis.

421
00:33:12,751 --> 00:33:16,994
[SPEAKER_01]: Even fleeting little thoughts, if they were correct, are going to be recognized instantly.

422
00:33:17,114 --> 00:33:18,275
[SPEAKER_01]: Because the basis is there.

423
00:33:21,217 --> 00:33:26,882
[SPEAKER_01]: So that's even when we said, oh, just think about Buddha, dhamma, saṅgha, recollection of virtue, you get samādhi as a result of it.

424
00:33:27,382 --> 00:33:33,107
[SPEAKER_01]: Because, yeah, the body behavior, by body and by speech, has been purified and that aggregate still persists.

425
00:33:34,007 --> 00:33:39,054
[SPEAKER_01]: Now, just tweak your thinking a little bit, focus on certain themes and pleasant abiding here and now.

426
00:33:41,518 --> 00:33:50,150
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what it also means, by the way, in the suttas when Buddha said mindfulness should remain always basically established upon the body and never abandoned.

427
00:33:51,422 --> 00:33:59,748
[SPEAKER_01]: The body, in terms of your sati and recollection, as if somebody's going with a sword behind you and you're carrying that pot full of water and everything is trying to distract you.

428
00:34:00,309 --> 00:34:05,533
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not about focusing on the sensations, it's about maintaining the right order, never slipping from it.

429
00:34:06,193 --> 00:34:17,422
[SPEAKER_01]: So, establish the right order of the body, to that extent necessary, and don't allow it to be perverted, even if there are dancers around you and everything else, because your head will be chopped off if you pervert the order, if you lose the mindfulness of the body.

430
00:34:17,942 --> 00:34:24,985
[SPEAKER_01]: If you lose the correct recollectedness of the body, the correct memory, the memory that doesn't pervert the order.

431
00:34:25,005 --> 00:34:26,225
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, memory of the right order.

432
00:34:26,265 --> 00:34:29,226
[SPEAKER_01]: Memory of the right order, yeah.

433
00:34:29,386 --> 00:34:34,728
[SPEAKER_00]: So, this is a short sutta and it seems to be in connection with what we're talking about.

434
00:34:35,548 --> 00:34:39,950
[SPEAKER_00]: I think you've probably already answered this, but maybe you can say something more.

435
00:34:42,216 --> 00:34:48,966
[SPEAKER_00]: It starts because when what exists, by assuming what, by adhering to what, does the thought occur?

436
00:34:49,227 --> 00:34:52,251
[SPEAKER_00]: I am superior, I am equal, or I am inferior.

437
00:34:55,830 --> 00:35:10,596
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the Buddha says, when there is the I, bhikkhus, by assuming the I, by adhering to that assumption of the I, the thought occurs, I am superior, I am equal, I am inferior, and so on, with the ear, nose, tongue, body and mind.

438
00:35:12,497 --> 00:35:19,039
[SPEAKER_00]: So, by assuming what, in terms of the senses, does one start to get this?

439
00:35:19,540 --> 00:35:20,500
[SPEAKER_01]: By assuming the wrong order.

440
00:35:21,740 --> 00:35:25,085
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what I mean by assuming the externals first.

441
00:35:25,125 --> 00:35:26,306
[SPEAKER_01]: You don't even see the internal.

442
00:35:26,426 --> 00:35:27,388
[SPEAKER_01]: You don't see the I.

443
00:35:27,588 --> 00:35:28,029
[SPEAKER_01]: You don't see.

444
00:35:28,069 --> 00:35:32,495
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you are the perceiver, the conceiver, which means you are now comparable there.

445
00:35:33,156 --> 00:35:33,796
[SPEAKER_01]: I am better.

446
00:35:34,017 --> 00:35:34,618
[SPEAKER_01]: I am worse.

447
00:35:34,858 --> 00:35:35,399
[SPEAKER_01]: I am equal.

448
00:35:35,999 --> 00:35:37,602
[SPEAKER_01]: But the point is, no, you are secondary.

449
00:35:38,673 --> 00:35:42,934
[SPEAKER_01]: And if you see yourself as secondary, there is no more conceit of superiority or inferiority.

450
00:35:43,375 --> 00:35:44,375
[SPEAKER_01]: No, you are out of the picture.

451
00:35:44,415 --> 00:35:46,496
[SPEAKER_01]: You don't exist for the eye or for the objects.

452
00:35:47,176 --> 00:35:47,956
[SPEAKER_01]: You're irrelevant.

453
00:35:48,716 --> 00:35:56,159
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you can't even be dejected on account of it, because dejection requires some recognition of you being sort of, you know, demoted or inferior.

454
00:35:56,259 --> 00:35:56,419
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

455
00:35:57,327 --> 00:36:01,831
[SPEAKER_01]: And there is no room for any conceit, because conceit comes as a result of conceivings.

456
00:36:02,091 --> 00:36:03,392
[SPEAKER_01]: But I'm not equal, then.

457
00:36:03,712 --> 00:36:04,433
[SPEAKER_01]: What is this?

458
00:36:04,473 --> 00:36:09,437
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, you're not even equal, because even equality, we are equals, requires me and you.

459
00:36:10,197 --> 00:36:21,666
[SPEAKER_01]: But if both you and I are utterly, completely invisible to our own I and sense of irrelevant, non-existent, redundant, then it's like, well, it's like comparing two things that are redundant.

460
00:36:22,527 --> 00:36:23,768
[SPEAKER_01]: You wouldn't say, oh, they're equal.

461
00:36:23,808 --> 00:36:25,930
[SPEAKER_01]: No, they're just both equally redundant, maybe.

462
00:36:30,355 --> 00:36:34,999
[SPEAKER_01]: So, yeah, conceit, you can take that, as I said before, it's it's more of a symptom.

463
00:36:35,680 --> 00:36:37,301
[SPEAKER_01]: Conceit is a symptom of a problem.

464
00:36:38,053 --> 00:36:39,294
[SPEAKER_01]: No, I must get rid of the conceit.

465
00:36:39,354 --> 00:36:43,197
[SPEAKER_01]: No, I'm... yeah, you must stop misconceiving, basically, the core of your existence.

466
00:36:43,277 --> 00:36:44,658
[SPEAKER_01]: You mean... you mean, like, pride?

467
00:36:44,758 --> 00:36:45,158
[SPEAKER_01]: Pride.

468
00:36:45,178 --> 00:36:45,459
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, yeah.

469
00:36:45,479 --> 00:36:45,739
[SPEAKER_01]: Pride.

470
00:36:45,879 --> 00:36:46,159
[SPEAKER_01]: Pride.

471
00:36:46,279 --> 00:36:46,720
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what I mean.

472
00:36:46,820 --> 00:36:47,580
[SPEAKER_01]: Superiority.

473
00:36:47,800 --> 00:36:48,381
[SPEAKER_01]: Superiority.

474
00:36:48,401 --> 00:36:48,761
[SPEAKER_01]: Pride.

475
00:36:48,841 --> 00:36:49,021
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

476
00:36:49,081 --> 00:36:52,384
[SPEAKER_01]: It's like a... that I'm better, I'm worse, I'm inferior.

477
00:36:52,604 --> 00:36:55,566
[SPEAKER_01]: All of that is the result of the problem that you're taking for granted.

478
00:36:56,667 --> 00:37:06,258
[SPEAKER_01]: And, eh... so, if you if you start, as I said, sense restraint, virtue, and then look for the correct practice of mindfulness of the body, that right order, your conceit will fade.

479
00:37:06,358 --> 00:37:08,240
[SPEAKER_01]: Doesn't matter how you might come across to other people.

480
00:37:08,540 --> 00:37:15,427
[SPEAKER_01]: The point is, internally, there is no ana... that anathimāni, what it says in the citta, like free from any arrogance and so on.

481
00:37:15,448 --> 00:37:16,429
[SPEAKER_01]: It's just that it's not there.

482
00:37:16,849 --> 00:37:28,876
[SPEAKER_01]: Because that's the result of sustaining that wrong order and wrong conceiving, where you are the perceiver, the conceiver of the world, which inevitably then results in, you know, creating a certain value around that.

483
00:37:29,056 --> 00:37:31,018
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm better, I can get even better, and so on.

484
00:37:33,579 --> 00:37:34,079
[SPEAKER_00]: And there's a...

485
00:37:37,421 --> 00:37:39,403
[SPEAKER_00]: I think this was from the Theragata.

486
00:37:40,043 --> 00:37:41,964
[SPEAKER_00]: Anyway, this is a...

487
00:37:44,857 --> 00:37:50,519
[SPEAKER_00]: Arahant, really, his name is Janta, he's the priest, the high priest's son, it was called.

488
00:37:50,719 --> 00:37:54,040
[SPEAKER_00]: And this is his poem in the Theragāta.

489
00:37:56,100 --> 00:38:00,121
[SPEAKER_00]: I was drunk with the pride of birth and wealth and authority.

490
00:38:00,761 --> 00:38:04,522
[SPEAKER_00]: I wandered about intoxicated with my own gorgeous body.

491
00:38:05,263 --> 00:38:08,524
[SPEAKER_00]: No one was my equal or my better, or so I thought.

492
00:38:09,764 --> 00:38:13,425
[SPEAKER_00]: I was such an arrogant fool, stuck up waving my own flag.

493
00:38:14,807 --> 00:38:21,032
[SPEAKER_00]: I never paid homage to anyone, not even my mother or father, nor others esteemed as respectable.

494
00:38:22,012 --> 00:38:24,974
[SPEAKER_00]: I was stiff with pride, lacking regard for others.

495
00:38:26,175 --> 00:38:37,163
[SPEAKER_00]: When I saw the foremost leader, the most excellent of charioteers, shining like the sun at the fore of the mendicant saṅgha, I discarded conceit and vanity.

496
00:38:38,104 --> 00:38:43,148
[SPEAKER_00]: And with a clear and confident heart, I bow down with a head to the most excellent of all beings.

497
00:38:44,109 --> 00:38:50,714
[SPEAKER_00]: The conceit of superiority and the conceit of inferiority have been given up and eradicated.

498
00:38:50,754 --> 00:38:55,838
[SPEAKER_00]: The conceit I am is cut off and every kind of conceit is destroyed.

499
00:38:55,938 --> 00:38:57,039
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, you become an arahant.

500
00:38:57,700 --> 00:39:02,303
[SPEAKER_00]: But by understanding the body... Well, exactly.

501
00:39:02,323 --> 00:39:04,085
[SPEAKER_01]: But seeing that actually this is...

502
00:39:05,828 --> 00:39:08,949
[SPEAKER_01]: There's nothing to be conceited about or feel inferior on account of either.

503
00:39:09,589 --> 00:39:15,630
[SPEAKER_01]: It is, as I said, your sense of self, your conceit is like... it's something your eye doesn't even know about.

504
00:39:16,310 --> 00:39:23,392
[SPEAKER_00]: Yet, here you are, you know, all important or all unimportant, all afraid, but your own body does... is not aware of you.

505
00:39:23,572 --> 00:39:26,452
[SPEAKER_00]: Look how wonderful I am on account of this thing that is not mine.

506
00:39:26,572 --> 00:39:27,432
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, yeah.

507
00:39:27,532 --> 00:39:34,674
[SPEAKER_01]: That has its own cause, that I kind of know, but I ignore because I'm intoxicated with the pleasure that I get momentarily from it.

508
00:39:35,663 --> 00:39:37,164
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why you develop these views as well.

509
00:39:38,044 --> 00:39:44,766
[SPEAKER_01]: If the conceit and sensual pleasures were not pleasant, nobody would be conceited or vain.

510
00:39:45,547 --> 00:39:57,871
[SPEAKER_01]: But you get pleasure on account of it, you take pleasure for granted, you put the pleasure first, you put the pleasure as the basis of your whole experience, and then you could be witnessing unpleasant things, and not see the nature of it, because you refuse to allow the order to change.

511
00:39:59,032 --> 00:40:00,472
[SPEAKER_01]: You still put the pleasure first.

512
00:40:01,393 --> 00:40:02,373
[SPEAKER_01]: You refuse to give it up.

513
00:40:03,523 --> 00:40:14,069
[SPEAKER_01]: Your body can be deteriorating, breaking down, and you still remain attracted to bodily pleasures, because you refuse to put them second, you refuse to see the body as first, because now it's too unpleasant as well to admit that.

514
00:40:14,690 --> 00:40:22,834
[SPEAKER_01]: The longer you admit, the longer you refuse to admit it, the harder it will be to do it later, because you're becoming more and more dependent on that wrong order.

515
00:40:23,395 --> 00:40:30,199
[SPEAKER_01]: Practically speaking, the burden is getting heavier, and it's crushing you more and more, and if you couldn't give it up so easily when it was relatively light,

516
00:40:32,687 --> 00:40:34,930
[SPEAKER_01]: So, don't wait till it's too late, in other words.

517
00:40:37,814 --> 00:40:43,301
[SPEAKER_01]: Because the intoxication grows, the more you engage with it, the more intoxicated you become.

518
00:40:45,043 --> 00:40:46,405
[SPEAKER_00]: The harder it will be to sober up.

